Quick install (Linux / macOS)
# Roboto Mono
wget -q "https://fonts.gstatic.com/s/robotomono/v23/L0xuDF4xlVMF-BfR8bXMIhJHg45mwgGEFl0_3vq_ROW4.woff2" \
     -O assets/fonts/RobotoMono-Regular.ttf
Quick install (Windows – PowerShell)
Invoke-WebRequest `
  "https://github.com/googlefonts/RobotoMono/raw/main/fonts/ttf/RobotoMono-Regular.ttf" `
  -OutFile "assets\fonts\RobotoMono-Regular.ttf"
Fallback behaviour
If no font file is present AssetLoader automatically searches common system font directories (DejaVu, Liberation, Ubuntu, Arial, Segoe UI). If none are found it falls back to OpenCV's built-in bitmap font with no crash or error.
